  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code with J = 4, L = 12, P = 67. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site pairs (c, t) for c < sigma[c] with its image under pi; each parent X row becomes one stabilizer generator, X on representatives and Z on partners. E = [[59, 51, 23, 61, 32, 43, 18, 28, 55, 65, 15, 24], [23, 64, 21, 63, 62, 25, 8, 16, 19, 12, 34, 37], [60, 15, 17, 28, 14, 40, 25, 47, 14, 43, 16, 51], [65, 8, 51, 1, 55, 44, 55, 26, 29, 4, 7, 13]], sigma = [11, 6, 8, 7, 9, 10, 1, 3, 2, 4, 5, 0], B = [2, 18, 31, 50, 33, 13, 18, 50, 31, 33, 13, 2].",
